From: Iscle <albertiscle9@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] env: mtd: do not release a device after lookup failure

setup_mtd_device() leaves its output pointer untouched on error. Skip
put_mtd_device() when lookup fails and only release the allocated buffer.
Otherwise a missing environment device passes an uninitialized pointer
to the MTD core and can trigger a BUG during boot.

Signed-off-by: Iscle <albertiscle9@gmail.com>
---
--- a/env/mtd.c
+++ b/env/mtd.c
@@ -157,7 +157,7 @@
 
 	ret = setup_mtd_device(&mtd_env);
 	if (ret)
-		goto out;
+		goto free_buf;
 
 	sect_size = mtd_env->erasesize;
 
@@ -192,6 +192,7 @@
 out:
 	put_mtd_device(mtd_env);
 
+free_buf:
 	free(buf);
 
 	return ret;
